WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.150
Spring had come once more to Green Gables.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.010
The maples in Lover's Lane were red budded

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:08.860
and little curly ferns pushed up
around the Dryad's Bubble.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.860
Away up in the barrens,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.930
in the slightly snowed out land,

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.420
the Mayflowers blossomed out.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:24.740
And then came the violets, and
Violet Vale was empurpled with them.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:39.070
And in a certain morning of June...

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.810
Everything is just like in that day.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.280
Good morning, Marilla.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.530
Marilla, do you know what day is today?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.230
No, I don't.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.310
Your headache again?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.280
Yes.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.740
Oh, Marilla!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.050
I do truly wish I could have had the
headache in your place.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.860
I would have endured it joyfully for your sake.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:20.250
Marilla, will you leave me in charge
of the house for today?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.020
What are you saying?
What about school?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.660
But today is a very special day.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.950
What is so special about today?

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.260
Nothing very special.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.450
But I really wish to help you today.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.900
Well, can I?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:45.750
Then I'll let you do the morning housework
and prepare breakfast.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:50.030
Oh, I feel so very glad to be
able to help you, Marilla!

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.030
Matthew, breakfast is ready!!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.850
All right.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.730
Oh no. I have to talk with Diana.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.410
What is the matter?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.510
I must tell her I'm not going to school.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.560
You don't need to miss school.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.850
I'm all right now.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.700
Please, Marilla...

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.990
Let me help you today.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:49.070
I'll clean the dishes when I return,
so don't be touching them.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.470
That child can take over your work already.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:03.870
She still makes some mistakes, but...
Children grow up really quick.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.600
You're right.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:14.990
Sometimes I try to remember how were
our lives before she was here.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:21.220
When did I began to think that Green Gables
would not be the same without her?

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.960
You're right.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.390
It's been already a year
but I'm still so happy.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:43.290
That's why I wish to help Marilla
for the whole day today.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.380
I understand. I'll tell Mr. Phillips.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.800
Thank you.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.540
It's already eleven o'clock.
I have to hurry.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.040
Everything is ready.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.700
I forgot the pie from yesterday.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.640
It'll taste better warmed up.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.780
When will Matthew come back?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.410
He should be here soon.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.890
I forgot Marilla's lunch.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.180
It's you, Anne? Come in.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.960
I think I dozed off a little.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.530
How is your head?

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.590
I feel better now.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:27.020
Here is your lunch.
I made it with warm milk.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:31.270
My, my, you're treating me like a patient.
I'm not really sick.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.960
It's not so bad, is it?

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.130
I've also prepared Matthew's lunch.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.490
I did it the way you instructed.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:42.150
Really? Then I'll have my lunch here.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.380
Yes, please take care of yourself.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.770
Then I'm counting on you.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:50.420
Don't forget to draw the tea.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:52.160
Don't worry.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.990
Oh, I'm sorry. I was giving lunch to Marilla.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.590
She seems to be better now.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.670
Well now, I'm glad.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:23.180
I think there's something missing, but...

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:27.270
Well now... These will do just fine.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.920
I warmed the milk for Marilla.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.560
Well, please enjoy the meal.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:43.190
Matthew, do you remember
what day is today?

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:49.360
Well now, didn't Queen Victoria's
birthday just pass?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.580
Oh!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.060
Are you feeling better?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.790
Thanks to you I'm feeling much better now.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.270
But you should take a good rest today.
Alright, Marilla?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.450
It's all right.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:33.080
I'm not used to doing nothing.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:38.750
And I thought there was someone in
school you wouldn't want to lose to?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:44.500
Now go study to your room
and let me do the rest.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.860
But...

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:54.230
I'll go study then.
But I'll prepare the dinner.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.860
Yes, thank you then.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.180
This triangle...

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:16.090
If this triangle was real, then
the area would be the same.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.590
I did it!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.510
I suppose you are Mr. Cuthbert
of Green Gables?

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:28.820
It really was you. I'm very glad to see you.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:33.660
I was beginning to be afraid
you weren't coming for me,

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.120
and I was imagining all the things
that might have happened to prevent you.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:41.780
You could imagine you were
dwelling in marble halls.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:02.500
I read of a girl once in a novel
who had a lifelong sorrow,

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.000
but it wasn't red hair.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:08.110
Her hair was pure gold rippling back
from her alabaster brow.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:13.030
Oh, Mr. Cuthbert! Mr. Cuthbert!! Mr. Cuthbert!!!

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.020
Anne.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:18.690
Anne.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.140
I'll put your clothes here.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.260
I've put your washed clothing there.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.210
Oh!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.250
You've helped me much by attending
to the work and letting me rest.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:45.680
Of course it wasn't exactly necessary to
starch Matthew's handkerchiefs.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:51.050
And most people when they put a pie in
the oven to warm up for dinner,

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.780
take it out and eat it.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.690
I forgot! I left the pie in the oven.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.280
My, my. It's too late now.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:01.160
I've done it for you already.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:07.200
I'm sorry. I wanted to be extra good today
because it's an anniversary.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.530
Anniversary?

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:13.370
Yes. Do you remember what happened
this day last year?

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.750
No, I can't think of anything special.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:22.680
It was the day I came to Green Gables.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:28.760
I shall never forget it.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.380
It was the turning point in my life.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:35.520
Of course it wouldn't seem so important to you.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:42.240
The same day today last year
Matthew brought me here.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.020
Are you sorry you kept me, Marilla?

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.620
No, I can't say I'm sorry.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:54.650
If you want to help with dinner then
hurry up and do your homework.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:56.730
Yes.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:33.450
Matthew Cuthbert, who's that?
Where is the boy?

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.460
You don't want me!

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:41.370
You don't want me because I'm not a boy!

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:54.660
I might have expected it.
Nobody ever did want me.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:18:01.330
I might have known
nobody really did want me.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:05.620
Oh, what shall I do?
I'm going to burst into tears.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:35.320
Well, well, there's no need to cry so about it.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.230
Yes, there is need!

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:39.950
You would cry, too!

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:46.410
If you were an orphan and had come to a
place you thought was going to be home

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.140
and found that they didn't want you
because you weren't a boy

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.050
you would cry too.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:56.930
Oh, this is the most tragical thing
that ever happened to me!

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.910
Well, don't cry any more. We're not going to
turn you out-of-doors tonight.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.560
What's your name?

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.000
Will you please call me Cordelia?

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:19.450
Call you Cordelia? Is that your name?

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:23.960
No-o-o, it's not exactly my name...

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.240
but I would love to be called Cordelia.

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:29.430
It's such a perfectly elegant name.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.690
I don't know what on earth you mean.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.740
If Cordelia isn't your name, what is?

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:42.240
Anne Shirley.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:46.560
But, oh, please do call me Cordelia.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:49.430
It can't matter much to you
what you call me

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:53.230
if I'm only going to be here
a little while, can it?

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:58.120
And Anne is such an unromantic name.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.180
Matthew, do you remember what day is today?

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.510
I'm asking you what day is today.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:27.970
Well now, Anne asked me
the same this afternoon.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:33.580
In this day last year,
Anne came to Green Gables.

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:39.170
Don't give me that. It's definitely today.

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:42.570
You brought her here, Matthew!

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.060
How could you forget?

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:50.090
Well now, it was today?

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:57.230
Shouldn't you do something for her?

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.910
Welcome back.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.490
Y-yes.

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:10.890
Would you like to take the sorrel
to Bright River after dinner, Anne?

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:16.260
Well... if you wish, that is.

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:18.870
Matthew, could you repeat that?

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:25.900
Well... would you like to take the sorrel
to Bright River after dinner?

00:22:29.060 --> 00:22:30.200
Matthew!

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:33.680
Matthew!

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:37.710
Matthew, you didn't forget?

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:42.180
You really didn't forget that today is
the day I came to Green Gables!

00:22:42.530 --> 00:22:44.610
Well, I...

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:51.240
Stop wasting time or it will be too dark, Anne.

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:53.670
Now come help me.

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:55.250
Marilla!

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:59.030
Are you coming too?
Let's all go to Bright River.

00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:01.540
No, I have no interest in that.

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:07.200
If I take the sorrel that persistent
headache of mine is not going to spare me.

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:09.770
You go along with Matthew.

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:15.430
Along that...  what did you call it...
White Way of Delight.

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:21.540
It should be full of beautiful apples now.

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:24.040
Just like one year ago.

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:26.060
Marilla!

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:29.600
Marilla!

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:32.130
Now, now. We'd better begin our dinner.

00:23:32.130 --> 00:23:34.850
Matthew has been waiting hungrily.

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:36.980
Thank you, Marilla.

00:24:17.860 --> 00:24:20.750
Mr. Phillips, the teacher of
avonlea school is leaving

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.880
and the new minister and
his young wife arrive.

00:24:23.880 --> 00:24:26.920
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:28.760
The Minister's Young Wife.

00:24:28.760 --> 00:24:30.280
Please watch!
